r_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":19,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-05-08T13:27:10Z","updated_at":"2013-09-05T14:19:21Z","due_on":"2013-05-18T07:00:00Z","closed_at":"2013-05-18T07:38:47Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2013-05-16T00:52:10Z","updated_at":"2013-05-17T07:56:12Z","closed_at":"2013-05-17T07:56:12Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi Guys,\n\nAm having an issue with thread safety and the use of DefaultCompositeByteBuf by multiple threads at once.\n\nCurrently our application creates a CompositeByteBuf (of up to 512MB in size when all underlying ByteBuf's are included), and we are passing this single ByteBuf off to a number of threads to have specific read-only actions performed. (There is no modification of the ByteBuf itself, the threads are just reading information from it). These operation include compression of the ByteBuf, hashing it (md5, sha256, etc), and string/keyword/byte[] searches, etc in separate threads.\n\nTo allow all threads to operate on the single buffer concurrently and independently, we are using `duplicate()` to create duplicate ByteBuf before passing the ByeBuf off to each thread. (This allows each thread to maintain it's own indexes/marks into the ByteBuf, and in theory should allow independent use of a shared CompositeByteBuf).\n\neg.\n\n``` java\nByteBuf buf = ...\nCompressionThread comp = new CompressionThread(buf.duplicate());\nHashThread hash = new HashThread(buf.duplicate());\ncomp.run();\nhash.run(); \n// wait for completion and get results.\n```\n\nHowever during thread execution we are getting `IllegalStateException(\"should not reach here - concurrent modification?\");` exceptions in `findComponent()` and `toComponentIndex()`, despite the ByteBuf being duplicated.\n\nFrom what we can gather, not all state information is being replicated, just the indexes and marks (which according to the javadoc is all `duplicate()` it does), however for composites, this doesn't allow for multiple threads to access the duplicates while sharing the underlying buffer?\n\nAlternatively, we could use copy(), but this duplicates all information, so we end up 3-4 copies of the original ByteBuf, which for us means instead of having 512MB shared between multiple threads, we end up with 4x 512MB buffers being used!\n\nThoughts, ideas or workarounds are greatly appreciated.\n\nPS. using Netty 4.0.0.CR3-SNAPSHOT from github.\n## \n\nRegards,\nDarran\n","closed_by":{"login":"trustin","id":173918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzkxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin","html_url":"https://github.com/trustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https: